e":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:52:26-08:00","id":1033696,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Can't wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:58:57-08:00","id":1033702,"title":"","content":"Crauc Gods and Void Creatures from SofC are semivampires as well, I wonder if blood sorcery none kindred vampires will get mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T21:28:14-08:00","id":1033873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1033702#post1033702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crauc Gods and Void Creatures from SofC are semivampires as well, I wonder if blood sorcery none kindred vampires will get mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be pretty suprised, they're not really significant creatures within the setting, just products of a couple specific Cruac abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T23:42:46-08:00","id":1033900,"title":"","content":"What I mean what more a statement on vamperic creations of blood sorcery in general, not specific creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:46:34-08:00","id":1034039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1033900#post1033900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean what more a statement on vamperic creations of blood sorcery in general, not specific creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, gotcha. Yeah, something like that might be cool. I've got my fingers crossed for a 2e update to Gargoyles, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:18:35-08:00","id":1034056,"title":"","content":"There's an argument to be made that things born of blood sorcery are <i>entirely <u>of</u></i> the Blood (and thus &quot;wholly damned&quot;), where the premise of the book seems to be more about entities whose natures are more... divided. While I'd also like to see more about beings tied to blood sorcery, and more <i>of</i> them, this doesn't quite seem to be the place. There's always room for pleasant surprises, though.<br /> - - -<br /> Glad to see that this's moving right along... I'm curious to see where dhampirs wind up going in 2e, and if ghoul families* and crone-independent mandragora might make an appearance again. And whether the Neglatu might show up somewhere in the revenant section, come to think of it. Sure we already have the rules, but it would be nice to see a 2e bloodline printed in a supplement and that would seem like a fitting detail to include for the poor starving things.<br /> <br /> *Maybe even <i>animal</i> ghoul families, if we're really lucky... There's something interesting about the idea of a vampire making an unliving breeding pets specifically for their kin. If they don't show up, though, it'd be easy enough to whip up some rules on the fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:24:11-08:00","id":1034061,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be using gh\u00fbls in an upcoming game. It would be cool to have some 2e update but, realistically, it's unnecessary and I can just alter what's needed on my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:50:48-08:00","id":1034184,"title":"","content":"This is exciting. I'm particularly curious to see if the key aspect of CWoD revenants (their innate vitae production) makes a comeback in any form. There have been a few homebrewed suggestions bouncing around these forums, so it could be done.<br /> <br /> Otherwise? Well damn, the whole rest of the book. All those critter-types getting a 2e treatment sounds delicious.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:10:26-08:00","id":1034200,"title":"","content":"Seems like it'd be counter to the whole &quot;burning all ingested vitae during the daysleep&quot; thing if they just generated vitae all on their own, wouldn't it?* But some special revenant-related merits, and maybe some extra optional rules, would be very welcome. Maybe the return of Larvae as well, either as a &quot;cousin&quot; to revenants, a result of revenants trying to Embrace (or as their equivalent to spontaneous Embrace, if we want to make things even more messy), or even just as a sort of in-world jargon for &quot;revenant draugr&quot;. They were all sorts of creepy-fun, and it'd be neat for them to get a nod again.<br /> <br /> *Now <i>dhampirs</i>, on the other hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:15:54-08:00","id":1034206,"title":"","content":"You might check out <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\">the Neglatu</a> for a little more on revenants before the book comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:21:15-08:00","id":1034209,"title":"","content":"<i>Half-Damned</i> will include some weirdities, but it's mainly focused on our headlining half-damned: ghouls, dhampir, and revenants. We have a future book coming up that will get into variations of the Blood, and of course <i>Wicked Dead</i> is still largely usable in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:16:38-08:00","id":1034371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034056#post1034056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an argument to be made that things born of blood sorcery are <i>entirely <u>of</u></i> the Blood (and thus &amp;quot;wholly damned&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, where the premise of the book seems to be more about entities whose natures are more... divided. While I'd also like to see more about beings tied to blood sorcery, and more <i>of</i> them, this doesn't quite seem to be the place. There's always room for pleasant surprises, though.<br /> - - -<br /> Glad to see that this's moving right along... I'm curious to see where dhampirs wind up going in 2e, and if ghoul families* and crone-independent mandragora might make an appearance again. And whether the Neglatu might show up somewhere in the revenant section, come to think of it. Sure we already have the rules, but it would be nice to see a 2e bloodline printed in a supplement and that would seem like a fitting detail to include for the poor starving things.<br /> <br /> *Maybe even <i>animal</i> ghoul families, if we're really lucky... There's something interesting about the idea of a vampire making an unliving breeding pets specifically for their kin. If they don't show up, though, it'd be easy enough to whip up some rules on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an excellent point, they're not kindred, but they are full vampires (although with Void Creatures I'm not 100% certain).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:20:25-08:00","id":1034373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034209#post1034209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Half-Damned</i> will include some weirdities, but it's mainly focused on our headlining half-damned: ghouls, dhampir, and revenants. We have a future book coming up that will get into variations of the Blood, and of course <i>Wicked Dead</i> is still largely usable in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div> I look forward to that future book. Both the Core and Secrets of the Covenants hinted at oddies, like the possibility the Oath of Matrimony could give other splats blood potentency as a trait and the core the Nameless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T05:37:03-08:00","id":1034531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034209#post1034209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Half-Damned</i> will include some weirdities, but it's mainly focused on our headlining half-damned: ghouls, dhampir, and revenants. We have a future book coming up that will get into variations of the Blood, and of course <i>Wicked Dead</i> is still largely usable in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>How similar will the dhampirs be to those from Wicked Dead?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:57:39-08:00","id":1034676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034200#post1034200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like it'd be counter to the whole &quot;burning all ingested vitae during the daysleep&quot; thing if they just generated vitae all on their own, wouldn't it?* But some special revenant-related merits, and maybe some extra optional rules, would be very welcome. Maybe the return of Larvae as well, either as a &quot;cousin&quot; to revenants, a result of revenants trying to Embrace (or as their equivalent to spontaneous Embrace, if we want to make things even more messy), or even just as a sort of in-world jargon for &quot;revenant draugr&quot;. They were all sorts of creepy-fun, and it'd be neat for them to get a nod again.<br /> <br /> *Now <i>dhampirs</i>, on the other hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a terminology confusion here between versions, sir.<br /> <br /> Do note: revenant families in Classic WoD are entirely different from the revenants of VtR. The former are what &quot;ghoul families&quot; became. The later are a new take and either hapless accidents or ravenous antagonists.<br /> <br /> Ghoul families are a fascinating concept, hinging as they do on both the blood mysticism of vitae and the longer view of unaging vampires. But, they are still not the same as VtM's revenants. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:13:10-08:00","id":1034689,"title":"","content":"I think the real question here is did they find an excuse to say &quot;Damned Half-Damned and Statistics&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:25:04-08:00","id":1034696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034531#post1034531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How similar will the dhampirs be to those from Wicked Dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>We took some of the core conflict/doom from <i>Wicked Dead</i>, but it's not a supernatural curse anymore -- there are plenty of interpersonal reasons for a vampire's kid to start or get into trouble with other vampires. We've got plenty of hooks detailing how that can unfold, and we deal with violent conflict, social conflict, and mixes of the two. The goal this time is to make dhampir viable player characters, rather than (by default) an antagonist.<br /> <br /> I should mention that I'm not developing this one. I'm overseeing it as Chronicles of Darkness lead, but on-the-ground development is in the hands of <i>Vampire</i>'s new line dev, Danielle Lauzon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:00:07-08:00","id":1034721,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:59:05-08:00","id":1034760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034676#post1034676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a terminology confusion here between versions, sir.<br /> <br /> Do note: revenant families in Classic WoD are entirely different from the revenants of VtR. The former are what &quot;ghoul families&quot; became. The later are a new take and either hapless accidents or ravenous antagonists.<br /> <br /> Ghoul families are a fascinating concept, hinging as they do on both the blood mysticism of vitae and the longer view of unaging vampires. But, they are still not the same as VtM's revenants.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>A-ah, I see. S'what I get for assuming I guess... looked them up real quick, and they do sound interesting. Could definitely see them being the end-goal of some long-term Ordo experiment or something, and if one or a handful did pop up I can only imagine how sought-after they'd be... fair bit of story potential there. Wouldn't mind seeing something like them in some form, maybe as an incredibly rare ghoul-family-specific merit or string of merits at the very least. Though of course we wouldn't want them to hew too closely to their Masquerade cousins, but there's room to fiddle with them and give them some unique traits.<br /> <br /> (Also, let's maybe not with the &quot;sir&quot; thing... disregarding matters of my identity, it also just feels a bit too formal for a forum setting.)<br /> <br /> - - - - - - - - - - -<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034696#post1034696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We took some of the core conflict/doom from <i>Wicked Dead</i>, but it's not a supernatural curse anymore -- there are plenty of interpersonal reasons for a vampire's kid to start or get into trouble with other vampires. We've got plenty of hooks detailing how that can unfold, and we deal with violent conflict, social conflict, and mixes of the two. The goal this time is to make dhampir viable player characters, rather than (by default) an antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that's interesting... even <i>more</i> curious to see how things pan out with them now, since as interesting as they were, their &quot;antagonist-first&quot; design did feel a bit restrictive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 01-19-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T14:22:30-08:00","id":1034862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034760#post1034760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Also, let's maybe not with the &quot;sir&quot; thing... disregarding matters of my identity, it also just feels a bit too formal for a forum setting.)<br /> <br /> - - - - - - - - - - -<br /> <br /> Ooh, that's interesting... even <i>more</i> curious to see how things pan out with them now, since as interesting as they were, their &quot;antagonist-first&quot; design did feel a bit restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blarg, yes. Apologies--in my defense all spare time recently has gone to setting research regarding knights, so it tends to slop over....<br /> <br /> And indeed, Rose's comment on dhampir makes them even more intriguing!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T06:59:21-08:00","id":1035199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1034696#post1034696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We took some of the core conflict/doom from <i>Wicked Dead</i>, but it's not a supernatural curse anymore -- there are plenty of interpersonal reasons for a vampire's kid to start or get into trouble with other vampires. We've got plenty of hooks detailing how that can unfold, and we deal with violent conflict, social conflict, and mixes of the two. The goal this time is to make dhampir viable player characters, rather than (by default) an antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>So would it be fair to say that they're no longer walking tutelary curses, but still a walking demonstration of how vampires are their own biggest reason for why they can''t have nice things?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:50:29-08:00","id":1035282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1035199#post1035199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would it be fair to say that they're no longer walking tutelary curses, but still a walking demonstration of how vampires are their own biggest reason for why they can''t have nice things?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about right, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:47:20-08:00","id":1035346,"title":"","content":"Dampyirs are new to VtR 2e, but Ghouls and, Reverants have rules already for playing them, so I'm curious as to what this book will add to them. <br /> <br /> Honestly I don't see any advantages to being a reverant over a Ghoul or full Vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:45:54-08:00","id":1035427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033492-half-damned-in-red-lines?p=1035346#post1035346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"